biome (0.3.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Handle SIGTERM/SIGINT with a clean shutdown (logout now runs the normal
    teardown and stops the `-s` command), and fix the Qt/GLib bridge losing
    an event source when a file descriptor number was reused
  * Fix Meta/Ctrl/Alt shortcuts (e.g. Meta+L to lock) not working while the
    window menu is open, and Meta then opening the main menu on release
  * Session lock: the Alt-Tab switcher, window menu and drag icon now sit
    below the lock screen instead of above it; window captures (ext-foreign-
    toplevel image capture) are blank while locked; a monitor plugged in
    during an abandoned lock shows the red rect; the pointer picks up the
    surface under it on unlock; new popups are refused while locked
  * Fix a monitor whose first modeset failed being treated as live: a
    rejected configured mode now retries with the monitor's preferred mode,
    and if that fails too the monitor stays disabled (and is reported so)
    instead of holding windows and layout space. The pointer now picks up
    the surface under it after being pulled back onto a remaining monitor
  * Fix layer-shell clients (e.g. another shell's panel) hanging when they
    unmap and re-map a surface, and stop reconfiguring every surface on the
    output twice whenever a new one appears (a notification popping up no
    longer makes every panel recommit). ext-foreign-toplevel-list now
    reports real titles and app ids from the start. Scanout fades only apply
    to full-output surfaces, others use an opacity fade
  * Fix X11 windows losing their frame (and shifting content) after leaving
    fullscreen; X11 windows no longer move or resize themselves while
    maximized, fullscreen or snapped, interactive resize respects their
    min/max size hints, and a title change that reused the old text's memory
    no longer skips the title-bar redraw; X11 clients changing their
    decoration hints now update live
  * Fix windows staying on the other monitor after a monitor dropped out and
    returned (e.g. a DPMS blank bounce): they now go back to it, unless you
    moved them meanwhile. Fix maximized windows staying a panel-height short
    when the usable area briefly shrank and recovered before the client
    acked the resize
  * Fix two windows showing as active in the taskbar after the last window
    was minimized or the screen locked; maximizing a fullscreen window no
    longer shrinks it while fullscreen; dragging a window that mapped
    maximized no longer jumps; Ctrl-Alt-Shift-arrow moves the active window,
    not an unseen one; `MoveToplevelToWorkspace` ignores out-of-range
    workspaces
  * Fix a crash opening the snap menu on a window that had just closed or
    hidden itself, a crash when the pointer left every monitor while
    dwelling at a snap zone, a ~36 KB icon leak per closed window, and a
    window mapped onto another workspace stealing keyboard focus while
    invisible (it is marked urgent instead); a window that hides and
    reappears now comes back as a fresh one (not
    maximized/fullscreen/snapped/minimized)
  * Fix global shortcuts with Shift+letter never firing and letter shortcuts
    dying under Caps Lock; `SHIFT+1` and `SHIFT+exclam` both match now
  * GlobalShortcuts portal: refuse bare-key shortcuts (no non-Shift
    modifier, other than F-keys, XF86 keys, Print/Pause) and triggers with
    empty parts like `CTRL+`; fix the `ListShortcuts`/`ConfigureShortcuts`
    signatures and export the interface `version`
  * Match global-shortcut key names case-insensitively, so lowercase
    triggers like `CTRL+escape` and `xf86audiomute` bind (only exact-case
    keysym names did before)
  * Fix a shortcut staying "held" when its keyboard was unplugged mid-press,
    and the seat still advertising a keyboard after the last one was removed
  * Fix an abort on exit (every time the greeter's biome hands off to the
    session): wlroots' listener asserts on teardown
  * Fix a crash when a window that hid itself without closing (unmapped)
    then asked to be minimized or maximized, and stop such hidden windows
    leaving their title bar on screen or staying in Alt-Tab
  * Fix a crash when a monitor was unplugged (or dropped out on wake) while
    the screen was locked, and a black lock screen when a disabled monitor's
    blank lock rect landed over another monitor
  * Fix the screen staying locked after a correct password when the lock
    started with every monitor off (Forest's lock-on-display-off): the
    `locked` event was never sent
  * Fix keystrokes typed on the lock screen going to a background app when
    one of its menus was open as the lock started, or to the panel once that
    menu closed; the lock screen now always gets the keyboard, including
    when its monitor is unplugged. The Alt-Tab switcher closes on lock
  * Fix a crash when an app bound a global shortcut without a description
    through the GlobalShortcuts portal

 -- Nicholas Yoder <nicholasyoder@proton.me>  Tue, 17 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0500

biome (0.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add content-type-v1 and alpha-modifier-v1 (clients can now set
    per-surface opacity).
  * Read the theme's [Palette]: it sets the app palette, and the
    window-snap and Alt-Tab highlight color now follows the theme's
    highlight color. Theme loading now comes from Forest's forest-theme
    library (new build dependency: forest-theme-dev).
  * Add a compositor-side window menu (restore/maximize, minimize, move,
    resize, always on top, move to workspace, close), opened by
    right-clicking the titlebar, clicking the titlebar icon, or a
    client-side-decorated app's own titlebar menu; styled by the theme's
    shared.css, shared with Forest.
  * Add always-on-top windows.
  * Add window snapping: drag a titlebar to a screen edge or corner (with
    a preview) to tile to a half, quarter or maximize, or right-click /
    press-and-hold the maximize button for a snap menu with layout icons.
  * Add ext-image-copy-capture-v1 with per-window and per-output capture
    sources; hidden (minimized or other-workspace) windows capture too.

 -- Nicholas Yoder <nicholasyoder@proton.me>  Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0500

biome (0.2.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Port to Fedora 45 and wlroots 0.20.
  * Fix a crash when a layer-shell popup was created (xdg_popup
    unconstraining now deferred to the initial commit).
  * Force DRM Broadcast RGB to Full; per-output rgb_range override in
    Biome.conf.

 -- Nicholas Yoder <nicholasyoder@proton.me>  Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0500

biome (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Protocols: xdg-activation-v1 (launchers can raise existing windows;
    unhonored requests mark the window urgent), wlr-data-control (clipboard
    managers), pointer-constraints and relative-pointer (games, 3D apps),
    pointer-gestures (trackpad swipe/pinch/hold), wlr-gamma-control (night
    light tools such as wlsunset), single-pixel-buffer, xdg-shell v6.
  * Decorations: load themes from external layered QSS (as shipped by
    Forest themes) with live reload on config change, and render at the
    output's scale so they stay sharp at fractional scales.
  * GlobalShortcuts: send Deactivated on the key's release so clients can
    tell a hold from a tap; idempotent BindShortcuts, readable trigger
    descriptions, and collisions with existing bindings rejected.
  * Enforce layer-shell keyboard_interactivity per spec, and focus popups
    on map only when grabbing or activated through xdg-activation.
  * Outputs: persist the last output-management apply to Biome.conf; keep
    reconnected outputs off until the next wake; close layer surfaces when
    their output is disabled.
  * Exit when the -s command exits, so Biome can host a greetd greeter.
  * Limit the Alt-Tab switcher to the active workspace.
  * Drop a fullscreen window below a newly focused window on its output.
  * Fix maximized/fullscreen windows flashing unmaximized on map.
  * Fix a crash when an Xwayland window toggles override-redirect, keep
    Xwayland popups above fullscreen windows, and leave splash screens
    undecorated and centered.
  * Fix layer-shell fade-ins jumping partway on large outputs.

 -- Nicholas Yoder <nicholasyoder@proton.me>  Mon, 09 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0500

biome (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First release: a fixed-policy floating Wayland compositor on wlroots 0.18,
    built as the compositor for the Forest desktop.
  * Window management: floating placement, maximize/fullscreen, Qt/QSS-themed
    server-side decorations, Alt-Tab switcher with previews, workspaces
    (ext-workspace-v1), window open/close fades.
  * Xwayland support.
  * Shell protocols: wlr-layer-shell, wlr-foreign-toplevel-management,
    ext-session-lock-v1, ext-idle-notify-v1, idle-inhibit,
    wlr-output-power-management, wlr-screencopy, cursor-shape-v1.
  * Outputs: wlr-output-management for live layout changes, hotplug
    handling, fractional scaling, layout persisted in
    ~/.config/Biome/Biome.conf with system drop-ins in /etc/biome/conf.d.
  * Global shortcuts via an org.freedesktop.impl.portal.GlobalShortcuts
    backend.
  * Logs at info level by default; set BIOME_DEBUG=1 for debug logging.

 -- Nicholas Yoder <nicholasyoder@proton.me>  Mon, 05 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0400
